[agent:result]     Creates a new table in the specified catalog and schema.
[agent:result] 
[agent:result]     To create an external delta table, the caller must have the **EXTERNAL_USE_SCHEMA** privilege on the
[agent:result]     parent schema and the **EXTERNAL_USE_LOCATION** privilege on the external location. These privileges
[agent:result]     must always be granted explicitly, and cannot be inherited through ownership or **ALL_PRIVILEGES**.
[agent:result] 
[agent:result]     Standard UC permissions needed to create tables still apply: **USE_CATALOG** on the parent catalog (or
[agent:result]     ownership of the parent catalog), **CREATE_TABLE** and **USE_SCHEMA** on the parent schema (or
[agent:result]     ownership of the parent schema), and **CREATE_EXTERNAL_TABLE** on external location.
[agent:result] 
[agent:result]     The **columns** field needs to be in a Spark compatible format, so we recommend you use Spark to
[agent:result]     create these tables. The API itself does not validate the correctness of the column spec. If the spec
[agent:result]     is not Spark compatible, the tables may not be readable by Databricks Runtime.
[agent:result] 
[agent:result]     NOTE: The Create Table API for external clients only supports creating **external delta tables**. The
[agent:result]     values shown in the respective enums are all values supported by Databricks, however for this specific
[agent:result]     Create Table API, only **table_type** **EXTERNAL** and **data_source_format** **DELTA** are supported.
[agent:result]     Additionally, column masks are not supported when creating tables through this API.
[agent:result] 
