[agent:result]       **NOTE** Byte limits are computed based upon internal representations of the result set data, and
[agent:result]       might not match the sizes visible in JSON responses.
[agent:result] 
[agent:result]       Statements executed with `EXTERNAL_LINKS` disposition will return result data as external links:
[agent:result]       URLs that point to cloud storage internal to the workspace. Using `EXTERNAL_LINKS` disposition
[agent:result]       allows statements to generate arbitrarily sized result sets for fetching up to 100 GiB. The
[agent:result]       resulting links have two important properties:
[agent:result] 
[agent:result]       1. They point to resources _external_ to the Databricks compute; therefore any associated
[agent:result]       authentication information (typically a personal access token, OAuth token, or similar) _must be
[agent:result]       removed_ when fetching from these links.
[agent:result] 
[agent:result]       2. These are URLs with a specific expiration, indicated in the response. The behavior when
[agent:result]       attempting to use an expired link is cloud specific.
[agent:result]     :param format: :class:`Format` (optional)
[agent:result]       Statement execution supports three result formats: `JSON_ARRAY` (default), `ARROW_STREAM`, and
[agent:result]       `CSV`.
[agent:result] 
[agent:result]       Important: The formats `ARROW_STREAM` and `CSV` are supported only with `EXTERNAL_LINKS`
[agent:result]       disposition. `JSON_ARRAY` is supported in `INLINE` and `EXTERNAL_LINKS` disposition.
[agent:result] 
[agent:result]       When specifying `format=JSON_ARRAY`, result data will be formatted as an array of arrays of values,
[agent:result]       where each value is either the *string representation* of a value, or `null`. For example, the
[agent:result]       output of `SELECT concat('id-', id) AS strCol, id AS intCol, null AS nullCol FROM range(3)` would
[agent:result]       look like this:
[agent:result] 
[agent:result]       ``` [ [ "id-1", "1", null ], [ "id-2", "2", null ], [ "id-3", "3", null ], ] ```
[agent:result] 
[agent:result]       When specifying `format=JSON_ARRAY` and `disposition=EXTERNAL_LINKS`, each chunk in the result
[agent:result]       contains compact JSON with no indentation or extra whitespace.
[agent:result] 
[agent:result]       When specifying `format=ARROW_STREAM` and `disposition=EXTERNAL_LINKS`, each chunk in the result
[agent:result]       will be formatted as Apache Arrow Stream. See the [Apache Arrow streaming format].
[agent:result] 
[agent:result]       When specifying `format=CSV` and `disposition=EXTERNAL_LINKS`, each chunk in the result will be a
[agent:result]       CSV according to [RFC 4180] standard. All the columns values will have *string representation*
[agent:result]       similar to the `JSON_ARRAY` format, and `null` values will be encoded as “null”. Only the first
[agent:result]       chunk in the result would contain a header row with column names. For example, the output of `SELECT
[agent:result]       concat('id-', id) AS strCol, id AS intCol, null as nullCol FROM range(3)` would look like this:
[agent:result] 
[agent:result]       ``` strCol,intCol,nullCol id-1,1,null id-2,2,null id-3,3,null ```
[agent:result] 
[agent:result]       [Apache Arrow streaming format]: https://arrow.apache.org/docs/format/Columnar.html#ipc-streaming-format
[agent:result]       [RFC 4180]: https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4180
